From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - bound Extrema_ExtSS::Points and
 Extrema_ExtCS::Points against the point sequence

Extrema_ExtSS and Extrema_ExtCS count their extrema with

  int Extrema_ExtSS::NbExt() const { ...; return mySqDist.Length(); }

and bound Points() against that count alone. Their analytic branches append a
distance with no matching point pair when the pair is parallel:

  myIsPar = myExtElSS.IsParallel();
  if (myIsPar)
  {
    mySqDist.Append(myExtElSS.SquareDistance(1));   // and nothing to myPOnS1/myPOnS2
  }

An equidistant family has no unique witness point, so there is nothing to
append, but NbExt() then reports 1 and Points(1, ...) passes its range test and
reads myPOnS1.Value(1) on an empty NCollection_Sequence. Extrema_ExtCS is the
same shape at Extrema_ExtCS.cxx:302-306 with myPOnC/myPOnS. Bound each Points()
against its own point sequence, which is the fix Extrema_ExtCC::Points already
carries.

The tighter bound changes nothing for a non-parallel result: mySqDist and the
point sequences are appended together in every other branch, so they are the
same length there.

Measured on macOS arm64 against V8_0_1 with both translation units
override-linked, two parallel Geom_Planes 5 apart and a Geom_Line 5 above a
Geom_Plane. Before: NbExt() is 1, SquareDistance(1) is 25, and Points(1, ...)
exits 139 in both classes. After: the same calls raise Standard_OutOfRange, and
two non-parallel controls report the same two extrema with the same coordinates
as before.

The reproducer is Scripts/repro/2840/probe.mm and the transcript is
Scripts/repro/2840/override-link-transcript.txt in the OCCTSwift repository.
OCCTSwift issue #2840; Extrema_ExtCC is #636.

diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.cxx
@@ -564,7 +564,9 @@ int Extrema_ExtCS::NbExt() const

 void Extrema_ExtCS::Points(const int N, Extrema_POnCurv& P1, Extrema_POnSurf& P2) const
 {
-  if (N < 1 || N > NbExt())
+  // NbExt() counts mySqDist; the parallel branch appends a distance with no matching point pair
+  // (an equidistant family has no unique witness), so bound against the point sequence instead.
+  if (N < 1 || N > myPOnC.Length())
   {
     throw Standard_OutOfRange();
   }
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.hxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.hxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.hxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtCS.hxx
@@ -92,6 +92,9 @@ public:
   Standard_EXPORT double SquareDistance(const int N) const;

   //! Returns the point of the Nth resulting distance.
+  //! Exceptions
+  //! Standard_OutOfRange if N is not in [1, NbExt()], or if N has a distance but no
+  //! representative point pair (a parallel curve/surface pair with an equidistant family).
   Standard_EXPORT void Points(const int N, Extrema_POnCurv& P1, Extrema_POnSurf& P2) const;

 private:
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.cxx
@@ -290,7 +290,9 @@ int Extrema_ExtSS::NbExt() const

 void Extrema_ExtSS::Points(const int N, Extrema_POnSurf& P1, Extrema_POnSurf& P2) const
 {
-  if (N < 1 || N > NbExt())
+  // NbExt() counts mySqDist; the parallel branch appends a distance with no matching point pair
+  // (an equidistant family has no unique witness), so bound against the point sequence instead.
+  if (N < 1 || N > myPOnS1.Length())
   {
     throw Standard_OutOfRange();
   }
diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.hxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.hxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.hxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/Extrema/Extrema_ExtSS.hxx
@@ -89,6 +89,9 @@ public:
   Standard_EXPORT double SquareDistance(const int N) const;

   //! Returns the point of the Nth resulting distance.
+  //! Exceptions
+  //! Standard_OutOfRange if N is not in [1, NbExt()], or if N has a distance but no
+  //! representative point pair (a parallel surface pair with an equidistant family).
   Standard_EXPORT void Points(const int N, Extrema_POnSurf& P1, Extrema_POnSurf& P2) const;

 private:
